# Everything the cluster reads is written with LF, whatever the machine that
# edited it does locally. A shell script that arrives with CRLF fails on Linux
# as "bad interpreter" - the carriage return becomes part of the name.
*           text=auto eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
